Subject: [PATCH] feat: Pile-On manual enrollment UI on the client's own
 Pile-On page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a "Manually enroll" button to PileOnPipeline's toolbar (skills/
pile-on/page.tsx) — the page an operator already visits to see this
client's Pile-On activity, rather than a new, separate screen. Same
two-step preview-then-confirm flow as the chat tools, calling the exact
same underlying functions (previewManualPileOnEnrollment,
enrollProspectInPileOn from chat-pile-on.ts) through a new nested API
route, so a duplicate-booking refusal or a missing-credential error reads
identically whether triggered from chat or from this modal.

The force checkbox only appears once a real warning exists (typically an
existing booking on file for that email) and must be checked before the
Confirm button enables — mirrors the chat system prompt's "only force
after explicit user confirmation" rule as an actual UI constraint instead
of a prompt instruction.

